#!/bin/bash -l
#
# QUIET RERUN, RAL CPU array: the hpc_ral_cpu interferometer cells of sma.
# Likelihood-lifecycle phase 2b interferometer campaign (autolens_profiling#469), quiet rerun of batch 1
# (RAL 413146): 14 leg(s). Human 2026-10-29: "do the reruns now".
# GENERATED by scripts/misc/campaigns/interferometer_p2b.py --write; edit the generator,
# not this file (the campaign test fails on a hand edit).
#
# WHY. Batch 1 ran all 38 RAL CPU legs at once on euclid-ral-compute-1 at a 1-minute load of
# 45-72, so the dashboard refuses every row as a trend point (hpc/release_sweep.conf
# RELEASE_SWEEP_LOADAVG_CAP=8, judged on the row's loadavg_at_import). This repeats the
# same legs (same scripts, flags, library tag and NPROC=8), each alone on its node.
#
# LIBRARY CODE. A private checkout of the five libraries at tag 2026.10.25.1 ($PYAUTO_PRIVATE_BASE,
# default /mnt/ral/jnightin/profiling/PyAuto_2026.10.25.1) is prepended to PYTHONPATH over the shared venv
# ($PYAUTO_HPC_BASE, default /mnt/ral/jnightin/PyAuto). The job refuses to run if a library imports
# from anywhere else or sits at another tag, and after each leg it checks the row's
# library_revisions equal the checkout's HEADs. AP_ROOT is the checkout this was submitted
# from (hpc/<batch>/../..).
#
# ROWS. Into the gitignored output/p2b_quiet/ tree (logs and walls.tsv in
# output/p2b_quiet_logs/), never over batch 1's output/p2b_batch1/ or committed rows.
# Parity stays batch 1's: the references are not rerun.
#
# MEMORY. --mem=64gb from batch 0's sacct MaxRSS (bounding instrument) x 1.5,
# at least 32 GB.
# One leg per array task on `ral`, each holding its node exclusively, throttled to
# %2 (whole 236/252-core nodes of a shared partition).
#
# WALL-BASIS: measured by batch 1. Each leg's wall is its own batch-1 leg's sacct Elapsed
# (RAL 413146, under load 45-72, so an upper bound on a quiet run). --time is
# 1.25x (the slowest leg, 366 s, plus the 1200 s quiet wait) plus
# 15 min of slack, rounded up to the next 30 min.
#   4 leg(s): delaunay jax_cpu_dense_fp64_nufft breakdown, delaunay jax_cpu_dense_fp64_nufft runtime, delaunay jax_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde breakdown, delaunay jax_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde runtime
#   cell: interferometer/delaunay/sma  device: ral_cpu  precision: fp64
#   source: measured-wall  wall: 366  ref: 413146_0,413146_1,413146_2,413146_3  measured-on: sma  headroom: 1.25  median: included
#   2 leg(s): delaunay numba_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde breakdown, delaunay numba_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde runtime
#   cell: interferometer/delaunay_numba/sma  device: ral_cpu  precision: fp64
#   source: measured-wall  wall: 124  ref: 413146_4,413146_5  measured-on: sma  headroom: 1.25  median: included
#   2 leg(s): mge jax_cpu_dense_fp64_nufft breakdown, mge jax_cpu_dense_fp64_nufft runtime
#   cell: interferometer/mge/sma  device: ral_cpu  precision: fp64
#   source: measured-wall  wall: 62  ref: 413146_6,413146_7  measured-on: sma  headroom: 1.25  median: included
#   4 leg(s): rectangular jax_cpu_dense_fp64_nufft breakdown, rectangular jax_cpu_dense_fp64_nufft runtime, rectangular jax_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde breakdown, rectangular jax_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde runtime
#   cell: interferometer/pixelization/sma  device: ral_cpu  precision: fp64
#   source: measured-wall  wall: 210  ref: 413146_10,413146_11,413146_8,413146_9  measured-on: sma  headroom: 1.25  median: included
#   2 leg(s): rectangular numba_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde breakdown, rectangular numba_cpu_sparse_fp64_wtilde runtime
#   cell: interferometer/pixelization_numba/sma  device: ral_cpu  precision: fp64
#   source: measured-wall  wall: 115  ref: 413146_12,413146_13  measured-on: sma  headroom: 1.25  median: included

#SBATCH -J p2b_quiet_ral_cpu_sma
#SBATCH --partition=ral
